# .trivyignore — accepted deviations for `trivy config`
#
# Each entry is an explicit, reviewed risk acceptance. Rationale lives in
# docs/adr/0007-security-hardening.md (see "Accepted deviations"). Keep this
# list short and justified; do not add IDs without a documented reason.

# DS-0026 — No HEALTHCHECK defined.
# The .devcontainer/Containerfile builds an operator *workspace*, not a
# long-running service. A HEALTHCHECK has no meaning here.
DS-0026

# KSV-0020 / KSV-0021 — Runs with UID/GID <= 10000.
# podinfo intentionally runs as its image's own non-root user (uid 100 app /
# gid 101). PSS `restricted` only requires non-root, not a UID > 10000; matching
# the image user avoids unexpected permission failures. Enforced via numeric
# runAsUser/runAsGroup (see apps/podinfo/deployment.yaml).
KSV-0020
KSV-0021

# KSV-0125 — Image from an untrusted registry.
# ghcr.io is GitHub's container registry (FOSS, trusted by this project); the
# check's default trusted list is Docker Hub-centric. The image is
# ghcr.io/stefanprodan/podinfo, pinned to 6.7.1.
KSV-0125
